[0m[32m
[0m[32mCompanies have several options at their disposal to thwart a corporate raider. The poison pill strategy prevents the raider from acquiring its stock by selling the stock to existing shareholders at a dramatically low price or by giving it to them for free. Another option is to sell the assets of the company, thereby lowering its value and making it less attractive for a takeover. With the "White Knight" strategy, the company under attack is bought by a friendly corporation or investor for a fair market amount. This keeps the company in business while taking it out of the corporate raider's reach. <|im_end|>[0m
